{
  "abstract": "We characterize normalized real and complex Hadamard matrices through the local extremum behavior of every tensor power of entrywise power energies. We construct almost flat real orthogonal matrices in every sufficiently large dimension with a quantitative rate, and give infinite families of strict local minima that do not attain the global minimum of quartic energy. We also obtain quantitative existence bounds for sign matrices with condition numbers approaching one, and a subpolynomial bound on the logarithmic deficit from Hadamard's maximal-determinant bound. See README.md for the main theorem statements, RESULTS.md for further results, paper/main.pdf for proofs and citations, and TECHNICAL.md for formalization coverage and build details.",
